==Environment and geography==
===Climate===
Axarquía has {{W|oceanic climate}} with very mild {{W|Mediterranean climate|Mediterranean}} ([[w:Köppen climate classification|Köppen]] ''Csb'') influences. The summer is essentially dry, but the city is affected by fogs from the {{W|Antarctic Circumpolar Current}} during most of the year. In the winter, rainfall can occasionally be extremely heavy when a powerful frontal system enters the [[Strait of Ivorra]], but frequency of such rains varies greatly from year to year. Monthly average temperatures vary just around 6°C between the coolest and the warmest month, from {{cvt|17|C}} in January to {{cvt|11.4|C}} in July. Snowfall occurs in the highest parts of the city. In winter, strong winds can lead to {{W|wind chill}} temperatures below freezing.

